From bd0cf5261c0c8bf23354263f01201081bbc46dbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Substring <frog2wah@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 23:35:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/40] Add a libretro driver to run software rendered libretro
 cores

* New "libretro" system loading the core given by -libretro_core with the content given by -libretro_content
* retro_run is called once per frame at VBLANK start, with no VBLANK period and VIDEO_UPDATE_AFTER_VBLANK so the frame is displayed right away
* The screen follows the geometry and refresh rate reported by the core, so switchres, frame delay and vsync apply as for any other system
* Hardware rendering (RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_HW_RENDER) is refused: no OpenGL or Vulkan context is shared with the core
* 0RGB1555, RGB565 and XRGB8888 pixel formats, stereo audio at the core sample rate
* 4 RetroPads with left analog stick
* MAME save states wrap retro_serialize, battery RAM saved to nvram/libretro/<content>.srm
* Core options defaults from the core, overridable in <libretro_system_path>/<core name>.opt
* Add libretro.h (MIT) from RetroArch

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
