Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:12:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/40] Add a Core Options menu and save libretro core options
 per core

* Add runtime_option_provider to running_machine: a system hosting an external emulator exposes its options, categories and values to the user interface
* New "Core Options" main menu entry (ui/coreopts), with a submenu per category, left/right to change a value, UI clear to restore the default, the help text of the selected option, and Reset System for options that apply on start
* The libretro driver keeps the full option definitions (v2, v1, intl and legacy variables), their visibility (SET_CORE_OPTIONS_DISPLAY and the update display callback) and reports changes to the core through GET_VARIABLE_UPDATE
* Core options are read from <libretro_system_directory>/<core name>.opt then <cfg_directory>/libretro/<core name>.opt, and written to the latter when changed, in the RetroArch format

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
