From 519bd75ddd3a38102dff8978e683974a6a87624c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Substring <frog2wah@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:47:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/40] Fix libretro content in zip and 7z archives

* MAME's image device handed a virtual path inside the archive, which cores reading the file themselves (need_fullpath) couldn't open
* Like RetroArch: cores opening archives themselves (block_extract, or zip/7z in their extensions) get the archive; otherwise the first file of the archive with an extension the core accepts is extracted, in memory, or to a temporary file deleted on exit for cores needing a path

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
