From: Substring <frog2wah@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:47:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/40] Support hardware rendered libretro cores on Windows

* Split libretro_gl into the common OpenGL part (framebuffer object, readback) and a platform context: EGL on Linux and other Unix systems, WGL on Windows
* WGL: opengl32.dll loaded at run time, context on a hidden window created with wglCreateContextAttribsARB in the version and profile the core asks for (OpenGL ES through WGL_EXT_create_context_es2_profile), the context of an OpenGL MAME renderer is restored after each call to the core
* GPU selection (-libretro_gl_device) is Linux only, WGL uses the default GPU
* Builds with MinGW but not tested on Windows yet

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
